From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:33:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm: share native transport and guest buffers

Port the fixed arena and guest-allocated MSM buffer contract used by
Droid-VM 899a4e179a5793c5aa86bbf0799b0683c6746422 and GunyahVM
1af844a to virglrenderer 1.3.0. Keep the current Venus and fence-sharing
implementations while exposing pool mapping offsets without changing
mapping ownership. Native DRM transport buffers reuse the boot-shared
arena, and guest-owned GPU pages arrive through a duplicated dma-buf.

TEST=ARM64 library and render-server build with Venus and MSM enabled
TEST=Pool fd offsets, capacity exhaustion, freeing and zeroed reuse
